            {
              "_type": "table",
              "caption": "Which format to choose",
              "headers": [
                "Format",
                "Best for",
                "Notes"
              ],
              "rows": [
                {
                  "_key": "k71",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "HTML",
                    "Checking entries on screen",
                    "Quickest way to look up a single deductor or quarter"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k73",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "PDF (Export as PDF from HTML)",
                    "Saving a dated copy for your records",
                    "Good to attach to your tax folder each year"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k75",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Text",
                    "Importing into tax or accounting software",
                    "Downloads as a compressed file"
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "_key": "k76"
            },
            {
              "_type": "callout",
              "type": "insight",
              "text": "A PDF opened through the portal often has no password. If a downloaded Form 26AS file does ask for one, it is your date of birth in DDMMYYYY format. For someone born on 15 April 1990, that is 15041990.",
              "_key": "k77"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k78",
              "_type": "collapsible",
              "title": "Another route: through your bank's net banking",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_key": "k79",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "k80",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "Several banks let you view Form 26AS from inside net banking, including State Bank of India, ICICI Bank, Axis Bank, Kotak Mahindra Bank and Bank of Baroda. Look for a tax or Form 26AS option in the menu.",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ],
                  "markDefs": []
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k81",
                  "_type": "block",
                  "style": "normal",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "_key": "k82",
                      "_type": "span",
                      "text": "This works only if your PAN is linked to that bank account. The data comes from the same TRACES records, so the content is identical to the e-filing route.",
                      "marks": []
                    }
                  ],
                  "markDefs": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "k83",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k84",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "When to Download, and Why You Will Do It More Than Once",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k85",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k86",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Form 26AS is not a document that is issued once. It is a live view of statements the department has processed so far. It changes whenever a deductor files a quarterly statement, files a correction, or the department finishes processing one.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_type": "table",
              "caption": "What Form 26AS for FY 2025-26 is likely to show, depending on when you look",
              "headers": [
                "If you download in",
                "Salary TDS you will probably see",
                "Why"
              ],
              "rows": [
                {
                  "_key": "k88",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Early May 2026",
                    "April to December 2025",
                    "Q4 statements are not due until 31 May"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k90",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Early June 2026",
                    "Most of the year, some Q4 gaps",
                    "Q4 statements filed near the deadline may still be processing"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k92",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "After mid-June 2026",
                    "Full year for most employers",
                    "Q4 statements processed and Form 16 issued by 15 June"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k94",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "After a correction",
                    "Updated figures",
                    "The deductor's correction statement has been processed"
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "_key": "k95"
            },
            {
              "_type": "bigIdea",
              "text": "Download Form 26AS twice: once when you start reconciling, and again on the day you file. Save both copies with the date in the file name.",
              "_key": "k96"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k97",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k98",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Common Problems and Fixes",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "What you see",
                "Likely cause",
                "Fix"
              ],
              "rows": [
                {
                  "_key": "k100",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Nothing happens after clicking Confirm",
                    "Browser blocked the TRACES pop-up",
                    "Allow pop-ups for incometax.gov.in and try again"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k102",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "No entries at all for the year",
                    "Wrong assessment year selected, or it is too early in the year",
                    "Check you picked financial year + 1, and try again after mid-June"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k104",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Your employer is missing entirely",
                    "Employer quoted a wrong PAN, or did not file statements",
                    "Check the PAN in Form 16 Part A and raise it with HR"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k106",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "Only some quarters appear",
                    "A quarterly statement is late, missing or still processing",
                    "Wait a week or two, then ask HR for the receipt numbers"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k108",
                  "_type": "tableRow",
                  "cells": [
                    "An entry you do not recognise",
                    "Someone quoted your PAN by mistake, or you forgot a payment",
                    "Note it for the next lesson. You may need to report it or have it corrected."
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "_key": "k109"
            },
            {
              "_type": "callout",
              "type": "insight",
              "text": "For income from tax year 2026-27 onward, this information is compiled as Form 168 under the Income-tax Act, 2025, together with what AIS shows. The first Form 168 relates to income earned from April 2026, so check the portal's menu when you prepare that return in 2027, as the path may differ from the steps above.",
              "_key": "k110"
            },
            {
              "_type": "toolLink",
              "label": "Income Tax e-Filing Portal: Login",
              "url": "https://eportal.incometax.gov.in/iec/foservices/#/login",
              "description": "Log in with your PAN or Aadhaar, then go to e-File, Income Tax Returns, View Form 26AS.",
              "_key": "k111"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k112",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k113",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Check Your Understanding",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_type": "exercise",
              "variant": "quiz",
              "title": "Pick the right year",
              "question": "Divya wants to check TDS on her salary for April 2025 to March 2026. Which assessment year should she select on TRACES?",
              "options": [
                "2024-25",
                "2025-26",
                "2026-27",
                "2027-28"
              ],
              "correctIndex": 2,
              "explanation": "Income earned in FY 2025-26 is assessed in AY 2026-27. Assessment year is always the financial year plus one.",
              "_key": "k114"
            },
            {
              "_type": "exercise",
              "variant": "fillInTheBlank",
              "title": "Crack the password",
              "textWithBlank": "Rahul was born on 9 March 1994. If his downloaded Form 26AS file asks for a password, he should enter ___.",
              "correctAnswers": [
                "09031994"
              ],
              "explanation": "The password is the date of birth in DDMMYYYY format, with leading zeros: 09 for the day, 03 for the month, 1994 for the year.",
              "_key": "k115"
            },
            {
              "_type": "exercise",
              "variant": "numericInput",
              "title": "What an early download shows",
              "prompt": "Rohit's employer deducts ₹13,500 of TDS every month from April 2025 to March 2026, and files every quarterly statement on the last possible day. Rohit downloads Form 26AS on 20 May 2026. How much salary TDS is he most likely to see?",
              "correctValue": 121500,
              "tolerance": 0,
              "unit": "₹",
              "explanation": "Statements for Q1 to Q3 (April to December) were due by 31 July, 31 October and 31 January, so 9 months are visible: 9 × ₹13,500 = ₹1,21,500. The Q4 statement for January to March is not due until 31 May, so ₹40,500 is missing for now.",
              "_key": "k116"
            },
            {
              "_type": "exercise",
              "variant": "scenario",
              "title": "Nisha finds nothing",
              "scenario": "Nisha, a nurse at a private hospital in Kochi, logs in to the e-filing portal in late June 2026, follows the steps and selects assessment year 2025-26. Her Form 26AS shows TDS that does not match the Form 16 she just received for FY 2025-26, and some entries are from an employer she left in 2024.",
              "prompt": "What has gone wrong, and what should she do?",
              "modelAnswer": "She has selected the wrong year. Assessment year 2025-26 covers income earned in FY 2024-25, which is why her old employer appears. For her FY 2025-26 Form 16 she needs assessment year 2026-27. She should go back to View Tax Credit, select 2026-27, and compare again. If the figures still do not match, she can move on to reading each part of Form 26AS, which the next lesson covers.",
              "_key": "k117"
            },
            {
              "_type": "exercise",
              "variant": "checklist",
              "title": "Do it now",
              "steps": [
                "Log in to incometax.gov.in with your PAN or Aadhaar.",
                "Go to e-File, Income Tax Returns, View Form 26AS, and confirm the redirect.",
                "Tick the terms, click Proceed, then View Tax Credit (Form 26AS).",
                "Select the assessment year for the income you are checking.",
                "View as HTML, then Export as PDF.",
                "Save the file with today's date in the name, for example Form26AS_AY2026-27_2026-06-20.pdf."
              ],
              "_key": "k118"
            },
            {
              "_type": "keyTakeaways",
              "points": [
                "Form 26AS is not emailed to you. Download it from the e-filing portal, which redirects to TRACES.",
                "The path is e-File, Income Tax Returns, View Form 26AS, then View Tax Credit on TRACES.",
                "Select the assessment year, which is always the financial year plus one.",
                "Form 26AS is a live statement. Download after mid-June, and again on the day you file.",
                "If a file asks for a password, it is your date of birth in DDMMYYYY format.",
                "Missing employers or quarters usually point to a wrong PAN, a wrong year or an unfiled statement."
              ],
              "_key": "k119"
            },
            {
              "_type": "callout",
              "type": "disclaimer",
              "text": "This lesson is for education only. Menu names and steps reflect the e-filing portal and TRACES as of September 2026 and may change as the department updates its systems. For your specific situation, check the portal's help pages or consult a chartered accountant.",
              "_key": "k120"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
